<section class="sa-hero"><div class="sa-hero-g"><div class="sa-hero-t"><p class="sa-k">A field guide to work bags</p><h1>The bag that goes to work with you.</h1><p class="sa-lead">Satchel is an independent guide to leather satchels, briefcases and work bags. We explain how they are made, how to choose one that fits your day and laptop, and how to care for it for decades.</p><a class="sa-btn" href="#wizard">Find your bag &darr;</a></div><figure class="sa-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1790802924908-90a85258eb5b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=720&h=820&q=75" alt="a man in a suit and trench coat holding a leather briefcase on a staircase" width="720" height="820" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div>
<ul class="sa-spec"><li><b>3</b>Ways to carry</li><li><b>4</b>Common leathers</li><li><b>12</b>Months of care</li><li><b>0</b>Products sold</li></ul></section>

<section class="sa-s"><div class="sa-w sa-anat"><div><p class="sa-k">Anatomy</p><h2>Parts of a satchel</h2><p class="sa-lead">Tap a number to learn what each part does and what to look for.</p><div class="sa-part" id="an-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="sa-dia"><svg viewBox="0 0 460 380" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M150 110v-34a80 50 0 0 1 160 0v34" fill="none" stroke="#7A4A26" stroke-width="10"/><rect x="40" y="110" width="380" height="250" rx="18" fill="#9A6236"/><path d="M40 128q0-18 18-18h344q18 0 18 18v92H40z" fill="#7A4A26"/><path d="M52 210h356" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="8 6"/><rect x="140" y="170" width="20" height="70" rx="4" fill="#5B361B"/><rect x="300" y="170" width="20" height="70" rx="4" fill="#5B361B"/><rect x="134" y="232" width="32" height="22" rx="3" fill="#C9A36A"/><rect x="294" y="232" width="32" height="22" rx="3" fill="#C9A36A"/><path d="M40 300h380" stroke="#5B361B" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 5"/><circle cx="20" cy="140" r="9" fill="#C9A36A"/><circle cx="440" cy="140" r="9" fill="#C9A36A"/></svg>
<button class="sa-pin" style="left:50%;top:12%" data-p="0">1</button><button class="sa-pin" style="left:22%;top:40%" data-p="1">2</button><button class="sa-pin" style="left:31%;top:64%" data-p="2">3</button><button class="sa-pin" style="left:70%;top:79%" data-p="3">4</button><button class="sa-pin" style="left:4%;top:37%" data-p="4">5</button><button class="sa-pin" style="left:88%;top:58%" data-p="5">6</button></div></div></section>

<section class="sa-s sa-dk"><div class="sa-w"><p class="sa-k">Know the family</p><h2>Five work bag shapes</h2><div class="sa-shapes"><div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M35 18v-6a15 10 0 0 1 30 0v6" fill="none" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="10" y="18" width="80" height="48" rx="5" fill="#9A6236"/><path d="M10 22h80v20H10z" fill="#7A4A26"/></svg><h3>Satchel</h3><p>Flap with straps or buckles, top handle and shoulder strap. Structured and classic.</p><dl><dt>Carry</dt><dd>Hand, shoulder</dd><dt>Laptop</dt><dd>Up to 14&ndash;15&Prime;</dd></dl></div>
<div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="40" y="6" width="20" height="10" rx="3" fill="none" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="8" y="16" width="84" height="50" rx="3" fill="#5B361B"/><rect x="45" y="30" width="10" height="6" fill="#C9A36A"/></svg><h3>Briefcase</h3><p>Rigid or semi-rigid with a single handle. The most formal option.</p><dl><dt>Carry</dt><dd>Hand</dd><dt>Laptop</dt><dd>13&ndash;15&Prime;</dd></dl></div>
<div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 12L50 2l42 10" fill="none" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="8" y="16" width="84" height="48" rx="4" fill="#7A4A26"/><path d="M8 16h84l-6 26H14z" fill="#9A6236"/></svg><h3>Messenger</h3><p>Long cross-body strap and a full flap. Good for cycling and busy commutes.</p><dl><dt>Carry</dt><dd>Cross-body</dd><dt>Laptop</dt><dd>13&ndash;16&Prime;</dd></dl></div>
<div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 26V8M70 26V8M30 8q20-10 40 0" fill="none" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3"/><path d="M14 26h72l-6 40H20z" fill="#9A6236"/></svg><h3>Tote</h3><p>Open top, two handles, soft sides. Quick to reach into; less protective.</p><dl><dt>Carry</dt><dd>Shoulder</dd><dt>Laptop</dt><dd>Needs a sleeve</dd></dl></div>
<div><svg viewBox="0 0 100 70" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="22" y="6" width="56" height="62" rx="10" fill="#5B361B"/><rect x="30" y="34" width="40" height="22" rx="4" fill="#7A4A26"/><path d="M22 18h56" stroke="#C9A36A" stroke-width="3"/></svg><h3>Backpack</h3><p>Weight on both shoulders. Best for heavy loads and long walks.</p><dl><dt>Carry</dt><dd>Back</dd><dt>Laptop</dt><dd>Up to 16&Prime;</dd></dl></div></div></div></section>

<section class="sa-s sa-paper" id="wizard"><div class="sa-w sa-wiz"><div class="sa-wiz-h"><p class="sa-k">Bag finder</p><h2>Three questions to your shape</h2><ol class="sa-steps" id="wz-s"><li class="on">Commute</li><li>Load</li><li>Dress code</li></ol></div><div class="sa-wiz-b" id="wz" aria-live="polite"></div></div></section>

<section class="sa-street"><div class="sa-w"><p class="sa-k">On the street</p><h2>How work bags are really carried</h2></div><div class="sa-row"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1790802924838-6c923e20756f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a man boarding a train with a leather briefcase" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The train commute.</b> One hand free for the rail; a top handle earns its keep.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1791114401475-a298eeab822c?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="a person carrying a leather bag past a cafe" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The walk to the office.</b> A shoulder strap lets you carry coffee as well.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794369190297-d8e6a0d6baa7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=680&q=75" alt="an older man holding a black briefcase on a crosswalk" width="520" height="680" loading="lazy"><figcaption><b>The crossing.</b> A slim case kept close is easy to manage in a crowd.</figcaption></figure></div></section>

<section class="sa-s" id="care"><div class="sa-w"><div class="sa-care-h"><div><p class="sa-k">Care calendar</p><h2>A year of looking after leather</h2></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792315042753-2d20002b8c42?auto=format&fit=crop&w=420&h=280&q=75" alt="a man repairing a black bag on a vintage sewing machine" width="420" height="280" loading="lazy"></figure></div><div class="sa-cal" id="cal"></div><p class="sa-cal-n" id="cal-n" aria-live="polite"></p></div></section>

<section class="sa-s sa-paper"><div class="sa-w sa-in"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1645276255969-680d5b62789d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="a black bag opened to show its zipped inner pocket" width="560" height="640" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="sa-k">Inside the bag</p><h2>A place for everything</h2><p class="sa-lead">A well-organised bag is lighter on your shoulder and kinder to its own lining. Our rule of thumb:</p><div class="sa-zones"><div><b>Back wall</b><span>Laptop or tablet, in a padded sleeve, nearest your body.</span></div><div><b>Main compartment</b><span>Documents, notebook and a folder, standing upright.</span></div><div><b>Front pocket</b><span>Pens, cards, cables and anything you reach for often.</span></div><div><b>Out of the bag</b><span>Liquids without a sealed bottle, loose keys, heavy chargers you don&rsquo;t need.</span></div></div><p class="sa-tip">Keep the loaded weight under about 10% of your body weight, and switch shoulders through the day.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="sa-s sa-dk"><div class="sa-w"><p class="sa-k">The catalogue</p><h2>Further reading</h2><ul class="sa-idx"><li><a href="work-bag-guide.html"><span>I.</span><b>Choosing a Work Bag</b><em>Shapes, leathers, hardware and construction, and what to check before you buy.</em><i>&rarr;</i></a></li><li><a href="laptop-bag-fit-guide.html"><span>II.</span><b>Laptop Bag Fit</b><em>Measuring your laptop, padding, weight and strap comfort for daily carry.</em><i>&rarr;</i></a></li></ul></div></section>

